<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    angr SAILR / Phoenix goto-reduction via return-tail duplication WITH a call
    (Basque et al., USENIX Security 2024 "SAILR"; ReturnDuplicatorLow /
    ReturnDuplicatorBase, max_calls_in_regions).

    morton 'my_message_callback' (x86-64, GCC) @ 0x403de7 (file vaddr 0x3de7,
    relocated to image base 0x400000).  An if/else-if cascade over the parsed
    command token has a shared epilogue 'free(v6); return;'.  The "Invalid Command"
    arm must skip the rest of the body and jump straight to that epilogue, so
    Ghidra's CollapseStructure must express that in-edge as an unstructured
    'goto label_4041d6;' with the epilogue 'label_4041d6: free(v6); return;'
    (CollapseStructure has no schema that duplicates a tail to avoid a goto).  angr
    emits zero gotos by duplicating the 'free(ptr); return;' epilogue into the arm,
    turning the cross-edge into a structured early return.

    This is the THIRD SAILR goto-reduction pass and is distinct from the two merged
    siblings, both of which decline this exact shape:
      * gotoreduce (return tail) REJECTS any call in the tail, so it cannot handle
        'free(v6); return;' (a return tail WITH a call);
      * crossjumprevert (non-return fall-through tail) explicitly declines a tail
        that ends in 'return'.
    With BOTH gotoreduce AND crossjumprevert on, the morton goto+label remain.
    Only 'taildup' removes them (matching angr's max_calls_in_regions=2 budget).

    Stage model: S8 "goto-quality" sub-stage.  The option-gated 'ActionTailDup'
    (option 'taildup', default-OFF) runs after ActionFinalStructure (and after the
    two sibling passes): it finds an unstructured 'goto T' (here a BlockGoto arm
    '{ stmts; goto label }') where T is a small single-successor basic-block chain
    ending in 'return' that may contain up to 2 calls (no STORE), and inlines that
    return tail in place of the goto (a print-tree copy of the same ops, no p-code
    cloned and def/use untouched), then clears T's now-unused label.  Each
    duplication is logged ('taildup: duplicated return-call tail ...').

    The PLT call targets (strtok/strlen/malloc/mosquitto_publish/strcmp/etc.) are
    outside this single-function chunk, so they render as unnamed 'sub_<addr>'
    calls; only 'free' (0x403890) is named, since it is the call inside the
    duplicated tail.  That is irrelevant to the goto metric.

    Pass 1 (option taildup off): the bug is present; one 'goto label_4041d6' and
    the 'label_4041d6:' definition (so 'goto label_' = 1, 'label_4041d6' = 2).
    Pass 2 (option taildup on): the goto and label are gone and the
    'free(v6); return;' tail is duplicated into the arm, so the combined 'free(v6)'
    count rises from one (pass 1) to three (one in pass 1 plus two in pass 2: the
    inlined early-return plus the shared fall-through epilogue).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x403de7">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x403de7" name="my_message_callback"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x403890" name="free"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option taildup off</com>
  <com>lo fu my_message_callback</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option taildup on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="angr-taildup #1 (bug, off): one residual goto to the shared free();return; tail" min="1" max="1">goto label_</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-taildup #2 (bug, off): goto label reference + label definition present, none on" min="2" max="2">label_4041d6</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-taildup #3 (fix, on): free();return; tail duplicated (1 free off + 2 free on)" min="3" max="3">free\(v6\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
